        "Date"
      ],
      "status": "draft",
      "status_note": "Shareable draft awaiting approval; named owner, backup, manager, coverage and approval date must be assigned before it is issued policy. Proposed service timings and the 15-minute absence checkpoint need management approval.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "section": "Role and working arrangements",
          "steps": [
            "Your responsibility is to keep online classes organised, students informed and recordings accessible. Coordinate with faculty, Accounts and Technical Support, and follow up until each assigned issue is resolved.",
            "Office hours: Monday to Saturday, 11:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. IST. Classes and events outside office hours need a named duty person. Sunday coverage is event-specific, not routine office support.",
            "Assigned staff: ____________________    Backup: ____________________",
            "Reporting manager: ____________________    Effective date: ____________________",
            "Priority order: live-class problems and student access first; attendance calls and urgent communication next; recording and academic follow-up next; clip cutting during allocated non-class time."
          ],
          "seq": 1,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #1 'Role and working arrangements'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Calls and WhatsApp communication",
          "steps": [
            "Answer student calls, return missed calls and respond to routine WhatsApp queries during office hours. Record unresolved requests and give the student a clear next-update time.",
            "Send the latest timetable, reminders, class instructions, approved changes and recording updates to the correct batch. Verify dates, times and recipients before sending. Use official institute accounts.",
            "Communicate personal attendance, marks and concerns privately. Share with registered guardians for under-18 students and with parents of adult students only under the agreed permission."
          ],
          "seq": 2,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #2 'Calls and WhatsApp communication'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Teachers classes and timetable",
          "steps": [
            "Confirm teacher availability, subject, topic and duration. Check batch and faculty clashes before preparing the timetable. Schedule each class correctly in Vacademy and communicate the confirmed timetable.",
            "Before each class, verify teacher readiness, student access and required notes or class sheets. Check that the session starts. Escalate a missing teacher or a failed class immediately.",
            "For a cancellation or change, obtain the required approval, arrange a replacement slot, update Vacademy and notify students and faculty. After class, obtain the actual topic covered and any unfinished work."
          ],
          "seq": 3,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #3 'Teachers classes and timetable'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Attendance and absence calls",
          "steps": [
            "Use Vacademy attendance records. Check late joins, approved leave and technical problems before marking an unexplained absence. Call students who have not attended, ask the reason and help them join if the class is ongoing.",
            "Record the call outcome, reason and next action. If unanswered, send a private follow-up and keep the item pending. Escalate repeated absences to the reporting manager and relevant faculty.",
            "The automatic absence notification does not replace the absence call. Suggested first attendance check: 15 minutes after class starts, subject to manager confirmation. Simultaneous classes require agreed backup coverage."
          ],
          "seq": 4,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #4 'Attendance and absence calls'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Recordings and LMS availability",
          "steps": [
            "Vacademy records and publishes classes automatically. Verify that each recording is complete, audible, playable and visible to the correct batch from the student-access view. Check the beginning, middle and end and investigate reported gaps.",
            "Use clear subject, topic, faculty and date labels. Keep recordings in the correct chapter sequence. Check for missing or duplicate entries.",
            "If automation fails, raise a technical issue and arrange authorised upload or publication. Do not mark the task complete until student access works. Preserve the original recording and coordinate a recovery lesson if no usable recording exists."
          ],
          "seq": 5,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #5 'Recordings and LMS availability'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Video clip cutting",
          "steps": [
            "Use faculty or Marketing timestamps, or flag useful explanations, shortcuts and FAQs. Cut the selected segment and trim dead time without changing the meaning.",
            "Remove private student information and unapproved student footage. Label the clip with subject, topic, teacher and date, and retain the source recording and timestamps.",
            "Obtain faculty approval for academic accuracy. Hand approved promotional clips to Marketing for captions, branding and publishing. Upload academic clips only to the authorised LMS section.",
            "This role covers basic cutting and trimming. Advanced editing and independent social-media publishing are outside scope."
          ],
          "seq": 6,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #6 'Video clip cutting'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Student onboarding and academic support",
          "steps": [
            "For new admissions, act after Accounts confirms payment. Verify login, correct course and batch access, timetable and communication-group membership. Explain where to find recordings, submit work and raise doubts.",
            "Late joiners start ongoing live classes immediately. Provide earlier recordings and materials for the enrolled batch and obtain faculty guidance on missed-topic priorities. Do not independently extend target-exam access validity.",
            "Collect approved notes, class sheets and DPP from faculty and upload them to the correct subject and chapter. Arrange homework reminders and follow up on non-submission. Track pending faculty checking and unanswered app doubts; faculty remains responsible for answers and evaluation."
          ],
          "seq": 7,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #7 'Student onboarding and academic support'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Tests reports and webinars",
          "steps": [
            "Coordinate two flexible weekly test windows shared across subjects. Obtain the approved paper and settings, check student access, send instructions and track non-attempts, pending evaluation and compulsory test discussion. Confirm whether test reminders need manual sending.",
            "After review, send app-generated performance reports privately. Check failed deliveries and arrange faculty follow-up for concerns. Use the release schedule approved by the manager.",
            "Assist the Saturday and Sunday webinars as rostered: reminders, joining support, recording checks and host-review collection. Hand counselling requests to Admissions. Do not promise academic counselling or fee exceptions independently."
          ],
          "seq": 8,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #8 'Tests reports and webinars'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Daily checklist and closing update",
          "steps": [
            "At opening: review missed calls, WhatsApp messages, pending issues, today’s timetable, faculty confirmation and previous recordings awaiting checks.",
            "Before and during classes: check readiness, send reminders, verify start and access, review absences and complete or assign absence calls.",
            "After classes: verify recordings, upload approved materials, follow up on missed classes and update unresolved issues. Cut clips only when priority work is covered.",
            "Before closing: confirm tomorrow’s timetable, return pending calls, hand over evening activities and assign an owner and next-update time to every unresolved item.",
            "Send this daily update to the manager: classes planned and conducted; absence calls and pending callbacks; recordings checked or missing; materials and clips completed; open issues; approvals needed; tomorrow’s risks and duty cover."
          ],
          "seq": 9,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #9 'Daily checklist and closing update'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Records escalation and authority",
          "steps": [
            "Use Vacademy as the academic source record. In the Actions tracker record: date, student or batch reference, task or issue, responsible person, due date, status and completion note. Avoid duplicating detailed marks or attendance.",
            "Escalate immediately when a class or test cannot run, students cannot join, a teacher is unavailable, or a privacy/security concern arises. Contact the relevant team and reporting manager; retain follow-up ownership until handover is acknowledged.",
            "Faculty owns teaching, academic counselling, doubt answers and checking. Accounts owns payment verification. The authorised approver decides refunds, discounts and extensions. Technical Support fixes systems. Marketing approves and publishes promotional content.",
            "The coordinator must not share passwords, expose student data, approve fee exceptions, delete source recordings or close unresolved issues merely because they were forwarded."
          ],
          "seq": 10,
          "source": {
            "path": "handover/outputs/online-operations/Elevate-Online-Coordinator-SOP.docx",
            "locator": "word/document.xml, Heading1 #10 'Records escalation and authority'"
          }
        },
        {
          "section": "Manager setup before issue",
          "steps": [
            "Confirm the assigned batches, backup and after-hours roster. Fill in escalation contacts and approve the absence-call checkpoint, response deadlines, recording-check deadline and report-sharing schedule.",
            "Manager approval: ____________________    Date: ____________________",
            "Staff acknowledgement: ____________________    Date: ____________________"
